body:
@crepesAlot  https://github.com/sailuh/kaiaulu/issues/230#issuecomment-2387559750

Well done! You are correct, thank you for checking with @daomcgill

Could you share the editable file if we need to extend in the future?

@beydlern  I think you are trying to fix a problem on the GitHub Notebook when the issue lies in the config file specification itself. 

@crepesAlot The image of the paths for download may actually be incorrect. The GitHub Downloader that is more current is sitting on a PR on this repo. 

The path forward lies here:

https://github.com/sailuh/kaiaulu/blob/a0b3619e602077f8299019f8955f88b973575dc9/vignettes/download_github_comments.Rmd#L52 

In GitHub, the endpoint that gives you "replies", i.e. literally our comments on this issue or a pull request, is the endpoint above. So save_path should be loading that. I do not know why the paths on the folder image do not include that, is the configuration file specification incorrect?

@carlosparadis Here is the updated file organization diagram, with the analysis file path being equal to the rawdata path below it.
![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a4890624-f1a1-4456-a6a5-d8b6aafe8d77)
I moved the tools input files back to the git_repo folder where they were originally and fixed the output analysis folder to be outside the rawdata folder.

Unfortunately I attempted that, but it seems there was a limit to how low I'm allowed to expand the google images, and am unable to add anything below the tools section. I was hesitant to start shrinking everything down to make it fit, but if you'd prefer that, I can do so.
@beydlern is waiting on my commit to create and update get functions for bugzilla and scitools understanding.
I wanted to make sure that the current folder organization is good and do the scitools understanding config section before making the commit.

@daomcgill For this one I would consider making two execs, one that annotates, and the other that can query the file. Annotating can take a long time depending on the size of the project, hence the split. 

Otherwise, I think this is good! We can take another pass once #313 is done. 

Thanks!
